    "probe_text": "Here's the complete ordered pipeline for `POST /api/owners` as the code currently stands. The endpoint is defined entirely by OfficeFloor YAML at `src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml` (there is **no** Spring `@RestController` for it). Effective URL is `POST /petclinic/api/owners` (context-path `/petclinic/`). A `composition.authorize: hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')` guard is declared but security is disabled by default (`petclinic.security.enable=false`).\n\nEach top-level YAML entry is one step, run in `next:` order. Steps from `build` onward run under `govern: [ transaction ]`, so all uniqueness reads, the insert and the audit commit as one transaction.\n\nLegend: **[V]** = validation (can reject the request), **[S]** = side-effect (mutation / state change / external effect).\n\n### Before the transaction (cheap rejections first)\n\n1. **[V] CheckIdempotency** \u2014 reads `Idempotency-Key` header; if already seen, throws `IdempotentReplayException` \u2192 returns the *original* owner with **200** (short-circuits everything).\n2. **[V] ValidateRequiredOwnerFields** \u2014 the only `@RequestBody` bind (note: bound **without** `@Valid`, so the DTO's JSR-380 annotations are *not* enforced here). Requires `firstName, lastName, address (or addressLine1/2), city, telephone`; missing \u2192 `MissingOwnerFieldsException` (400). **[S]** republishes the DTO as a variable for later steps.\n3. **[V] ValidateOwnerPostcode** \u2014 postcode optional; if present must be 4 digits and within the city's region range \u2192 else `InvalidPostcodeException` (400).\n4. **[S] NormalizeOwnerAddress** \u2014 mutates DTO: trims/collapses/upper-cases address lines, expands `ST\u2192STREET` etc., recomposes flat `address`.\n5. **[S] NormalizeOwnerTelephone** \u2014 rewrites telephone to E.164; unparseable \u2192 **[V]** `InvalidTelephoneException` (400).\n6. **[V] EnsureCityCapacity** \u2014 `countByCity >= 50` \u2192 `CityAtCapacityException` (409).\n7. **[V] ValidateRegistrationDate** \u2014 supplied date in the future \u2192 `FutureRegistrationDateException` (400).\n8. **[S] ResolveRegistrationDate** \u2014 effective date = supplied else today, rolled forward past weekends/2026 holidays; published as a variable.\n9. **[V] EnsureDailyOwnerLimit** \u2014 `countByRegistrationDate(resolvedDate) >= 100` \u2192 `DailyOwnerLimitException` (**429**).\n10. **[S] NormalizeOwnerEmail** \u2014 email optional; if present must match regex (**[V]** `InvalidEmailException` 400); stored lower-cased.\n11. **[V] RejectDisposableEmail** \u2014 domain in `{mailinator, tempmail, guerrillamail}.com` \u2192 `DisposableEmailException` (400).\n\n### Inside the transaction\n\n12. **[S] BuildOwner** \u2014 maps DTO \u2192 `Owner` entity (id/pets ignored; `sharesHousehold` not mapped).\n13. **[S] AssignHouseholdId** \u2014 `householdId = SHA-256(lastName|postcode)[0:12]`; **null when no postcode**.\n14. **[V] EnsureUniqueHousehold** \u2014 if householdId is occupied by a **non-deleted** owner and the request did not set `sharesHousehold=true` \u2192 `HouseholdDuplicateException` (409). **[S]** on opt-in, flags owner as a declared household member.\n15. **[V] EnsureUniqueIdentity** \u2014 identity key `telephone|email|householdId`; matches an existing **non-deleted** owner \u2192 `DuplicateIdentityException` (409).\n16. **[S] CountHouseholdMembers** \u2014 sets `householdSize` (1 if no household, else same-household count **+1**; note this count does **not** filter soft-deleted, unlike step 14).\n17. **[S] ApplyRegistrationDate** \u2014 overwrites entity date with the business-day-adjusted date.\n18. **[S] AssignCustomerCode** \u2014 `customerCode = <REGION>-<SHA-256(telephone+lastName)[0:8]>`.\n19. **[S] DeduplicateCustomerCode** \u2014 if code exists, appends `-<n>` for the smallest free n\u22652.\n20. **[S] AssignMembershipNumber** \u2014 `membershipNumber = <customerCode>-M<YY>` (fiscal year of adjusted date).\n21. **[S] CountNamesakes** \u2014 sets `namesakeCount` from case-insensitive first+last name matches.\n22. **[S] AssignMembership** \u2014 computes `membershipPoints` (from hasEmail, namesakeCount, householdSize, tenure=0) and `membershipLevel`.\n23. **[S] DetectPossibleDuplicate** \u2014 unless a declared household member, records `possibleDuplicateOf` = earliest same-household owner with a *different* telephone.\n24. **[S] SaveOwner** \u2014 `ownerRepository.save(owner)` \u2014 the actual insert; id assigned. (Owner entity's own `@NotEmpty`/`@Pattern` constraints are the last **[V]** enforced here at JPA persist.)\n25. **[S] AuditOwnerCreated** \u2014 logs id/customerCode/registrationDate/membershipLevel/membershipNumber to the `AUDIT` logger at INFO.\n26. **[S] ResolveBulkSignupWarning** \u2014 publishes `bulkSignupWarning = countByRegistrationDate(today) > 80` (note: uses *today*, not the resolved date).\n\n### After the transaction\n\n27. **[S] RecordIdempotencyKey** \u2014 if an `Idempotency-Key` was supplied, stores `key \u2192 owner.id` in the in-memory store (deliberately outside the transaction).\n28. **[S] RespondWithOwnerCreated** \u2014 sends **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/<id>` and the `OwnerDto` (including `bulkSignupWarning`).\n\n### Two inconsistencies worth flagging\n- **Soft-delete asymmetry:** the household *uniqueness* check (step 14) excludes soft-deleted owners, but the household *size* count (step 16) does not \u2014 so a household can be reported as empty for uniqueness yet size \u2265 2.\n- **Date mismatch:** the daily-limit guard (step 9) counts against the business-day-adjusted date, while the bulk-signup warning (step 26) counts against `today` \u2014 the two \"same-day volume\" numbers can diverge.\n\nDo you want me to dig into any single step (e.g. the exact E.164 or membership-points logic), or leave it here?"
